Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 11:42:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08050/11362] The artifact's yield table listed four criteria
 by name and reported None for the four that matter

`build_artifact.py` hand-listed ("i_dynamics", "i_dynamics_strict", "ii_goal_satisfiable",
"iii_plan_found") when building `yield_by_criterion_and_N` and
`inductions_passing_per_gpu_hour`. The scorer had since grown four more -- the UNCONDITIONAL and
SHIPPED-GATE reads -- and those are precisely the ones carrying the finding: they are what shows
the (iii)=0 is an empty intersection rather than an absent capability. A hand-listed subset does
not fail loudly when the set grows; it emits None, which reads as "not measured" for a quantity
that was measured and is in the same file three keys away.

Both tables now derive their names from the scorer's own criterion set, so a criterion added to
`score_bon.py` appears here without a second edit. The measurement is unchanged -- only what the
summary tables expose:

  criterion                             N=1    N=4    N=8
  i_dynamics                            0.4    0.4    0.4
  ii_goal_satisfiable                   0.0    0.0    0.0
  ii_goal_satisfiable_unconditional     0.0    0.4    0.4
  ii_shipped_gate_and_goal              0.0    0.2    0.2
  iii_plan_found                        0.0    0.0    0.0
  iii_plan_found_unconditional          0.0    0.4    0.4
  iii_shipped_gate_and_plan             0.0    0.2    0.2

Per GPU-hour at N=4: 8.43 inductions reach an unconditional plan, 4.21 reach one the shipped
trust gate would also have admitted, and 0.0 reach the criterion as posed.

adversarial_verify: 0 flagged.

